# Line endings, pinned deliberately.
#
# The .skill packages are built byte-for-byte from the sources in .claude/skills/,
# and a drift check compares the two. If a working tree carries CRLF while git
# stores LF, every bundle looks drifted on a fresh clone and CI fails for a reason
# that has nothing to do with the change. So the sources are LF everywhere,
# regardless of anyone's core.autocrlf.
.claude/skills/** text eol=lf

# The packages are zip archives. Git must never rewrite a byte inside one.
*.skill binary

# Everything else: normalise in the repo, leave the working tree to the platform.
* text=auto
